<p>These terms apply to authorised government users of GOV.UH Forms.</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Use the service for authorised government work</h2>
<p>You must use GOV.UH Forms only for a service or function your organisation is responsible for. Creating or publishing a form does not create legal authority to collect information or make decisions.</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Security</h2>
<p>Use an authorised work account, a suitably managed device and a trusted connection. Follow your organisation's security requirements and report suspected compromise through its incident-management route.</p>
<p>Do not use GOV.UH Forms to collect information that your organisation or the Forms platform is not authorised or equipped to handle.</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Completed form data</h2>
<p>Before publishing, make sure completed submissions have an approved receiving route, access controls, records arrangements and any safeguarding or escalation process required by the service.</p>
<p>Check submitted information before relying on it. A technical form check does not establish that information supplied by a user is accurate.</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Data protection</h2>
<p>Your organisation is responsible for the information it collects through its forms. You must provide accurate privacy information and follow the applicable information-management and data-protection requirements.</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Accessibility and service quality</h2>
<p>Use the standard Forms components correctly, write clear content and test the complete service journey before publication. The service-owning organisation remains responsible for its service assurance and the accessibility of the content it publishes.</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Changes to these terms</h2>
<p>Government Digital Service may update these terms when the GOV.UH Forms service or its operating requirements change. The current terms are published on this page.</p>
